    "physical_description": null,
    "summary": "Cloth of rectangular format  composed of 29 very narrow strips of handspun white and indigo-dyed cotton, hand-woven and  hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The warp is of indigo alternating with slightly narrower lines of white cotton; the weft is also primarily of indigo but with narrow lines of white. The sides of the strip are of indigo, and when sewn together make a broader band of indigo than elsewhere. Along each end of the cloth have been sewn a single thin light indigo edging strip that runs across the warps. This serves as a hem.",
